From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:44:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(groups): boot the peer member gateway on an api_server
 port it owns

test_peer_member_on_another_gateway_joins_replies_stops_recovers_and_is_revoked
flaked on CI with "timed out after 30s waiting for groups.capabilities": the
member gateway's room_link never enabled. The fixture picked the member's
api_server port free (bind, close) long before the daemon booted; under the
parallel runner another test's daemon can bind it first. The member then parks
api_server (api_server_port_in_use), still reports ready, and room_link stays
{'enabled': False, 'reason': 'api_server_required'} forever. Squatting the
picked port reproduces the exact failure.

The member's first boot now goes through api_daemon, which writes the config
for each picked port and re-boots only on that race; later boots keep the port
(the home's stored route names it) and assert the listener is theirs. The
room_link wait uses RPC_DEADLINE (a hang bound that returns as soon as the
link is enabled) instead of 30 s, so a CPU-throttled cold boot does not trip it.
